Solarkermis
Ingredients: GABBER + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Bassoon
Creative Catalyst: Descends from nomadic carnival musicians who perform exclusively during the fleeting minutes of a total solar eclipse.

Solarkermis is an apocalyptic fairground hallucination: blistering 210-BPM distorted gabber kick drums slammed headfirst into hyperactive, jovial acoustic contrabassoon runs, screaming wooden double-reeds, and ecstatic calliope fanfares designed to out-shout the sudden daytime dark.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 195–230 BPM. Relentless, four-on-the-floor gabber kicks overlaid with frantic, skipping 12/8 polka syncopations and staccatissimo bassoon flutter-tonguing.
- Harmonic Palette: Radiant Lydian and Mixolydian modes slammed into dissonant multiphonic growls; joyful, carnival-scale brass fanfare progressions that resolve with brassy, overdriven ecstasy.
- Production Signatures: "The Bocal Overdrive" (piezo pickups clamped to bassoon bocals driven through vintage Dutch gabber distortion racks); "Corona Gating" (hyper-fast rhythmic sidechain mutes that mimic strobe flashes of eclipsed sunlight); "Calliope Bleed" (high-pressure fairground steam-organ whistles captured via binaural field recordings and pitch-shifted into stadium rave leads).
- Dynamics: Zero gradual builds; violent, instantaneous dropouts where solitary wooden reed chatter gives way to deafening, 220-BPM wall-of-sound explosions that maintain ecstatic hysteria for three unbroken minutes before collapsing into absolute silence.

Scene & Origin Lore
The movement traces its roots to the Zonne-Kermis, an itinerant guild of Dutch-Flemish fairground mechanics, woodwind virtuosos, and illegal rave sound-system crews who have spent generations calculating global paths of totality. Traveling in painted wooden caravan wagons fitted with pressurized pneumatic pipes, they descend unannounced upon coastal salt marshes and open polders hours before an eclipse. The moment the moon begins eating the sun, the crowd—clad in grease-stained harlequin jumpsuits, heavy Dutch wooden clogs fitted with rubber hakken-soles, and ultraviolet eclipse goggles—gathers around towering wooden sub-bassoon rigs. They dance the Hakke-Vogel, an exhausting, joyful jumping ritual intended to jump-start the dying celestial furnace, fueled by warm jenever gin and the sheer terror-ecstasy of midday darkness.

Typical Instruments
- Custom Amplified Contrabassoon & Heckelphone: Fitted with copper bocals, contact mics, and high-gain fuzz pedals.
- Roland TR-909: Overdriven through analog guitar amplifiers and preamps to generate seismic, distorted kick drums.
- Pneumatic Fairground Calliope: Steam-driven carnival pipe organ played via modified MIDI solenoids.
- Amplified Wooden Ratchets & Anvils: Hand-cranked percussive noisemakers used to reinforce snare rolls.
- Roland JP-8000: Firing euphoric supersaw arpeggios that double the bassoon hooks in shrill octaves.

For Fans Of: Paul Elstak, Igor Stravinsky (The Rite of Spring), Angerfist, Partyraiser

